> and it doesn't look like crowning has any specific effect on getting
> sacrifice rewards (other than incrementing u.ugifts by one, which
> doesn't look like it would have THAT big of an effect), am I missing
> something?

AFAIK, you only get artifact gifts when you make sacrifices and your prayer 
timeout is zero (i.e. you see nothing or a four leaf clover after a 
sacrifice).  Being crowned greatly increases your prayer timeout, so most of 
your sacrifices will yield a "hopeful feeling".  You have to sacrifice/wait 
long enough for no more hopeful feelings.  Once you've gotten past that 
point, you'll get magicbane eventually, just don't pray or you'll have to 
start the whole process over.

